      "text": "```yaml\n- id: DR-01\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow fleet technicians to add new drones to an operating fleet.\n- id: DR-02\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow fleet technicians to retire drones from an operating fleet.\n- id: DR-03\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow fleet technicians to configure and record charging pads at sites.\n- id: DR-04\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow fleet technicians to send drones to charging pads to charge.\n- id: DR-05\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow fleet technicians to remove drones from service for repairs and return them to service after repairs are finished.\n- id: DR-06\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record and maintain a history of all drone maintenance, servicing, and repairs that can be presented to regulators.\n- id: DR-07\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow the platform airspace desk to manage the network of flight corridors between sites and the zones grouping them.\n- id: DR-08\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow the platform airspace desk to enter planned airspace closures with a specified start and end time, as well as sudden closures that take effect immediately.\n- id: DR-09\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow the platform airspace desk to amend existing closures during the day, including widening the affected area or changing the end time.\n- id: DR-10\n  requirement: >\n    The service must calculate and report the disruption caused across customer operating companies whenever a closure is entered or amended.\n- id: DR-11\n  requirement: >\n    The service must support delivery missions that transport a load from one site to another site.\n- id: DR-12\n  requirement: >\n    The service must support inspection missions that send a drone equipped with specified sensors to visit a list of points in a defined order and return to the starting site.\n- id: DR-13\n  requirement: >\n    The service must identify and show the dispatcher which available drones belonging to their company can reach the starting point of a job.\n- id: DR-14\n  requirement: >\n    The service must require a licensed dispatcher to select the drone, select the flight corridor, and sign off on the flight before the drone departs.\n- id: DR-15\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not autonomously choose a drone or a flight corridor for a flight.\n- id: DR-16\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow a dispatcher to call off a flight.\n- id: DR-17\n  requirement: >\n    The service must correctly process drone status reports that arrive late, out of order, duplicated, or not at all due to poor radio coverage.\n- id: DR-18\n  requirement: >\n    The service must handle instructions sent to drones and charging equipment idempotently, ensuring duplicate transmissions cause no unintended effects.\n- id: DR-19\n  requirement: >\n    The service must support continuous mission tracking when a drone restarts its software in flight following a fault and carries on flying.\n- id: DR-20\n  requirement: >\n    The service must preserve active flight and airspace operational state across server crashes, updates, and restarts during working hours.\n```",
